 "statement": "Annotated blind from the Beinecke scan only: canvas 1006203 ('71v and 72r', a foldout with four circles); f72r3 is the rightmost circle (centre near x=7030, y=1460 of the full image), and its ring counts match the label-line structure of f72r3 exactly (circular text lines .1, .14, .26, .34; label lines .2-.13, .15-.25, .27-.33). Outer ring: 12 nude female figures; middle ring: 11; inner ring: 7. None stands in a tub or barrel; each has an eight-pointed star with a yellow centre, often held on a line from the hand; figures are drawn radially with the head toward the rim, so lower ones look inverted. One inner figure wears a spiky crown-like headpiece. The centre holds two elongated many-legged animals with claws, one pale green with red claws above, one red below, with a word beneath. A brown stain at the fold hides part of the outer ring near 1-2 o'clock. No label line id is assigned to a figure: line ids carry no position and the blind rule forbids reading the label words; each figure carries its ring, angle and clockwise order and its ring's label line ids as candidates. The word beneath the centre animals has no label line of its own in the line-id list.",
